## Scaffolding a new React Native project

Getting started with React Native is a straightforward process. The React Native project creation tool ( [expo](https://docs.expo.dev/more/expo-cli/)) can be used to create a new React Native project with a sample file to help you get started. To create a new React Native project, execute the following command from your terminal:

```
npx create-expo-app react-native-paystack
```

After running the above command, let’s install the [Paystack package](https://www.npmjs.com/package/react-native-paystack-webview) we’d be making use of

```
yarn add react-native-paystack-webview
```

We’d also need to install a React Native package, which allows us to render web content in our application.

```
